# Normalize line endings so regenerating data files doesn't show up as a
# whole-file rewrite.
#
# The pipeline's CSVs are written by pandas, which emits CRLF on Windows. The
# `text` attribute makes git store LF in the repository and convert on the way
# in and out, so an unchanged rerun produces a clean diff and the repo stays
# portable.
#
# Note: `text` deliberately does NOT carry `eol=lf` here. Forcing LF in the
# working tree makes every pandas-written CSV permanently disagree with its
# checked-out form, and `git status` then reports the file as modified even
# though the normalized content is identical (verified: same blob hash, empty
# diff). Letting the checkout use the platform's native ending keeps status
# honest while still storing LF in the repo.

* text=auto

*.py    text
*.csv   text
*.md    text
*.txt   text
*.json  text

# wayfair_page.html is the scraper's input and the project's only copy of the
# real page. Keep its bytes exactly as saved -- never normalize it.
*.html  -text

# Binary artifacts: no line-ending translation, no textual diffs.
*.docx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.xlsx  binary
